From: rosy port
Subject: [PATCH] 1022 vincecache=2 (no cache cleaning at a submit); what the GPU path costs, in the log

Every submit cleaned the cache of every pooled buffer it named, whole: screens and textures of 5 MB each at
every glFlush of the window server, four or five a frame. That is a cost per pass that does not get smaller
with a faster GPU clock (8 to 10 ms a pass at 400 MHz as at 100). vincecache=2: the window server maps its
buffers write-combined again and a submit cleans nothing; the display still reads through a cached mapping of
the kernel, cleaned first. vincecache=1 is unchanged.

The VINCE FB line now also says the time since boot (its own seconds are ticks), whether the presenter thread
shows the frames (1021), how many and how long; a VinceGPU line follows with submits, the time in them and in
cleaning, cpu_prep and fence waits, and what the display waited.

